Objective: {{task}}

Step 1 of the ladder: orient. List the workspace, read the existing Go sources, and run `go doc` on the package you will extend. Learn the package's name, what it already owns, and the naming and comment conventions its existing code follows. Write nothing yet.

When you can name the package, its existing types, and the convention you will match, call `advance`.

Step 3: settle the field set. Read the struct as it stands and decide whether its fields are complete and correctly typed for the objective. Add, remove, or retype fields, then judge again.

Choose `revise` if you changed anything and want another pass. Choose `confirmed` only when you would defend this exact field set as final.

Objective: {{task}}

Step 6: implement the bodies, one function at a time, following the comment plan already written. Keep the plan comments only where they still explain something a reader could not see; delete the rest. Remove every `panic("not implemented")` you implement.

Choose `another_struct` only if implementing revealed that a second type is genuinely required; that returns you to step 2 for that type.

Objective: {{task}}
